Spec: the FRM queue, revised after reading where FRM does its work (owner review, 2026-10-23)

FRM 1.5.4 serves its API on one uWS thread. Only RequiresGameThread() endpoints (getPlayer, getResourceNode)
run on the game thread; getFactory, getBelts, getLifts, getPipes and the train endpoints don't. So the queue now:
- has two priority lanes (live before world), still one request in flight;
- lets getPlayer pass a large parse;
- skips the parse of a world layer whose raw body is unchanged;
- drops the factory-window rule.
tick-cost measures getResourceNode, the one large game-thread endpoint.

